@format 1
@id media-loading.common.viewer-gate
@title Viewer gate
@section Media loading
@area Common
@entry viewer-source-request
@summary Trace PViewerSourceOpen from command gating and sidecar resolution through preview-engine selection and backend request preparation.
@related media-loading.common.backend-load, media-loading.in-edit-tab
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag viewer

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias librarian = Cadroue.Application.LLibrarian
@alias preference = Cadroue.Application.LPreference

[viewer-source-request] Viewer source request <input>
= A Source request or tab-specific adapter called PViewerSourceOpen with a candidate path.
> viewer-gate

[viewer-gate] Viewer source gate <decision>
- Reject while viewer commands are inactive or source is blank; otherwise detect whether the source is a Cadroue sidecar @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
  @ librarian.LLibrarianFileCheck(...)
? "Blank or command-inactive" > viewer-stop
? "Sidecar source" > sidecar-resolve
? "Direct media source" > direct-ready

[viewer-stop] Viewer rejects request <output>
= PViewerSourceOpen returns immediately and no backend request begins.

[sidecar-resolve] Sidecar source resolution <decision>
- Resolve the recorded source, optionally accept a discovered mismatch, or ask the user to locate and verify the media file @ viewer.PViewerSidecarResolve(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerSidecarFind(...)
? "Media source resolved" > source-join
? "Read failed or source declined" > sidecar-stop

[direct-ready] Direct source accepted <junction>
> source-join

[sidecar-stop] Sidecar resolution ends <output>
= PViewerSourceOpen returns without changing the last-media preference or starting backend loading.

[source-join] Resolved source convergence <junction>
> remember-source

[remember-source] Last-media preference <storage>
- Store the resolved source as the last-media preference @ preference.LPreferenceMediaSet(...)
> reset-transform

[reset-transform] Incoming transform reset <process>
- Reset rotation and flip to defaults for the incoming source @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
> select-engine

[select-engine] Preview engine selection <process>
- PPlayerVideoLoad calls PViewerEngineSelect before backend loading; PViewerEngineRead returns the configured renderer engine only when PViewerEditEligible is true, otherwise it forces Flyleaf @ viewer.PViewerEngineSelect(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerEngineRead(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerEditEligible
> request-ownership

[request-ownership] Viewer request ownership <decision>
- Advance load serial, stop the viewer clock, clear inactive resume, pause the current player, then recheck lifetime and command activity before preparing the backend request @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
? "Still command-active/current" > expected-path
? "Became inactive or superseded" > preparation-stop

[expected-path] Expected completion path <storage>
- Normalize and store the expected source path, falling back to the original path when normalization throws, then start LMediaLoadAsync without awaiting it @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
> map:media-loading.common.backend-load

[preparation-stop] Viewer preparation abandoned <output>
= The load serial was advanced but LMediaLoadAsync was not started because the viewer became inactive/superseded during preparation.
